      en: "Uherské Hradiště is the heart of Moravian Slovakia (Slovácko), a rich ethnographic region known for its vibrant folklore, wine tradition, and hospitality. The royal town was founded in 1257 by King Ottokar II Přemysl and is situated on the Morava River. Its historic center is well-preserved and invites leisurely strolls. The city is a significant cultural hub, manifested in numerous events, most notably the Summer Film School, one of the largest film festivals in the country. Nearby are important pilgrimage sites like Velehrad. The vineyards on the slopes of the White Carpathians shape the landscape and the way of life for the people in the region."
