      en: "Hodonín, located on the border with Slovakia on the Morava River, is primarily known as the birthplace of Tomáš Garrigue Masaryk, the first president of Czechoslovakia. His native house and a museum dedicated to him are among the main attractions. The city is also a center for oil and natural gas extraction in the Czech Republic, a tradition dating back to the early 20th century. Additionally, Hodonín has established itself as a spa town with a modern spa specializing in iodine-bromine brine. The Baroque chateau houses an art gallery. The city is an important transport hub and the economic center of the southeasternmost corner of Moravia, a region rich in folklore and winemaking traditions."
